flowchart LR
	APPLY["two additional listeners, both registered at apply<br/>and both opt-in, gated at runtime on the scope cells"]
	FLIP["flipping a scope lands through the P10 volatile-refresh<br/>without any re-registration"]
	TRES["the tool-results arm on tools/post-execute<br/>with { prepend: true }, outermost vs the ccr hook's own prepended gate"]
	CCRGUARD["the CCR marker guard makes any load order safe<br/>the ccr compression sees the normalized bytes"]
	RULES["accepted, non-value-carrying decisions only<br/>text blocks only, N = 0 a true no-op with no ledger line<br/>fail-open"]
	BATCH["the step-batch arm on agent/pre-step in default order<br/>while scopes.batch is on, every incoming batch is normalized"]
	ONESHOT["the command's one-shot arm fires once regardless of the scope value<br/>cleared after one use - text blocks only, never the assistant/tool history"]
	LEDGER["the hook-dsh-normalize-ellipsis overpass ledger lines<br/>for N above zero only"]
	CMD["the normalize-overpass command, registered through the<br/>commands service when present - probe-once, a missing<br/>service simply skips the registration"]
	DECLINE["files paths declined - the sweep is owned<br/>by the normalize-file hook"]
	APPLY --> TRES
	APPLY --> BATCH
	APPLY ~~~ FLIP
	TRES --> RULES
	TRES -. "the marker guard" .-> CCRGUARD
	TRES --> LEDGER
	BATCH --> ONESHOT
	BATCH --> LEDGER
	CMD -. "batch arms it" .-> ONESHOT
	CMD -. "results on or off flips scopes.toolResults<br/>via the settings service, never direct State mutation" .-> TRES
	CMD -. "files paths" .-> DECLINE

